# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so anything git checks out gets CRLF in
# the working tree -- and `fly deploy` builds the image from the WORKING TREE,
# not from a git archive. Files below are read by Linux inside the container,
# where a trailing \r is not whitespace but part of the token:
#
#   * crontab   -- supercronic hands each line to /bin/sh, so a CRLF entry runs
#                  `python scripts/observe_listings.py\r` and fails with a
#                  "not found" that names a command you can see is present.
#                  Silent: supercronic keeps running, the job just never works.
#   * Dockerfile / *.sh -- same class of failure in RUN/CMD lines.
#
# These are currently LF and must stay LF through every clone and checkout.
crontab   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
